  "narrative": "All newly reported estimates were read in the signed direction supplied by the controller. No new claim has a signed lower bound that supports a scientifically meaningful difference of roughly 10% or more in the relevant dependency scale. The approximate 10% absolute effect size is about 0.025 for most outcomes whose mean is near -0.25, about 0.04 for SMARCA2, and about 0.01 for NFE2L2 because its mean is closer to zero. H14 is not supported: the KRAS-by-TP53-loss interaction is negative relative to the claimed stronger KRAS effect, with an interval that only marginally reaches the KRAS 10% scale; I leave it unresolved but deferred rather than active because the point estimate opposes the hypothesis. H15 is rejected: in TP53-wildtype cells the ERBB2-amplification effect on ERBB2 dependency is small and opposite the hypothesized direction, and its interval is below the ERBB2 10% threshold. H16 remains unresolved but deferred: the RB1-loss interaction for MDM2 is wide and imprecise because the RB1-loss cells are small, and the point estimate opposes the claimed direction; it does not justify further allocation now. H17 is rejected: conditional ARID1A loss among SMARCA4-wildtype cells has a near-zero estimate and an interval well below the SMARCA2 10% scale. H18 is rejected: the Avana-library interaction for SMARCA4 loss is small and negative, and its interval does not support a stronger SMARCA2 effect in Avana relative to non-Avana; the accepted SMARCA4-SMARCA2 association does not appear to be specific to Avana in this dataset. H20 remains unresolved but deferred: TP53-loss modification of the very strong KEAP1-NFE2L2 effect has a positive but small point estimate with an interval crossing zero; because the main KEAP1 effect is large and this is an exploratory interaction, I do not make an accept claim. H21, H22, H24, and H36 are rejected/closed as direct null or near-null associations. H23 remains unresolved but deferred: RB1 loss has a tiny positive signed effect on KIF18A dependency whose upper bound can reach a ~10% relative difference, but the point estimate and biology are not compelling enough for active follow-up. H37 remains unresolved but deferred for similar reasons; EGFR amplification is not supported for TMED10 dependency in a meaningful way, and the original EGFR-dependency claim was already rejected after validation. Overall, this wave strengthens the conclusion that the only robust dataset associations are the four large effects already accepted, while most oncogene-context and new-outcome hypotheses are null or underpowered. I request independent validation for H2 because KRAS mutation remains the most biologically plausible unresolved direct dependency association: its discovery interval includes a ~10%-scale stronger KRAS effect, but the point estimate is small; independent validation can either confirm a modest effect or close this hypothesis. The registered SMARCA4-by-ARID1A interaction is a focused refinement of the accepted SMARCA4-SMARCA2 association, testing combinatorial SWI/SNF loss after ARID1A main and conditional effects were null. These remain dataset-specific associations, not causal or generalizable claims.",
  "research_notes": "Current accepted dataset-level associations: SMARCA4 loss -> much stronger SMARCA2 dependency; MSI-high -> much stronger WRN dependency; TP53 loss -> weaker USP7 dependency; KEAP1 loss -> much weaker NFE2L2 dependency. These are supported by signed estimates far exceeding the ~10% relative threshold and intervals excluding clinically small effects. Rejected/closed include BRAF V600E with BRAF dependency, ARID1A main and SMARCA4-wt conditional effects on SMARCA2, original KEAP1 direction, MYC amplification with POLR2A/RPL11/DHX9/STAT3, ERBB2 amplification in TP53-wt cells, Avana-library modification of SMARCA4 effect, RB1 loss with KIF18A as an active follow-up, KRAS mutation with RIT1 dependency, STK11 loss with KRAS dependency, and several near-null direct associations. Newly deferred but not rejected because intervals can admit small meaningful effects or cells are too small: KRAS dependency by KRAS mutation is being independently validated; KRAS-by-TP53 interaction; MDM2-by-RB1 interaction; KEAP1-NFE2L2 by TP53 interaction; RB1 loss with KIF18A; EGFR amplification with TMED10; ERBB2 overall and adenocarcinoma subgroup are lower priority. The next priority is the H2 validation. If validation supports KRAS dependency, consider H26 adenocarcinoma refinement only if context matters. If null, close KRAS direct and likely subtype refinements. Registered refinement for next wave: SMARCA4 loss interaction with ARID1A loss on SMARCA2 dependency, motivated by accepted SMARCA4 effect and null ARID1A effects. Continue to avoid interpreting broad research markers/signatures unless they show robust large effects, because their assigned biology is unspecified.",
